Subject: Recharged: the main menu's Online button says PLAY ONLINE
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

Always on, without a switch, like the RECHARGED logo (tweak patch 0022).

The main menu's Online button (main_menu_v3.fen, Online _Menu_Item) shows the
localization key 0x1455335C, NINTENDO Wi-Fi CONNECTION in English (CONNEXION
Wi-Fi NINTENDO, CONEXIÓN Wi-Fi DE NINTENDO, NINTENDO WFC in German, two lines
in Japanese). Nintendo's service is gone: the button opens Recharged's online
play, and with Override retail menus its PLAY ONLINE page.
TLTextInstance::GetString and Render ask mscharged_tweak_loc_text
(src/platform/game_tweaks.cpp) for each localized text they look up; for this
key it gives PLAY ONLINE, in every language (Recharged's own texts are
English; the Japanese texts use the same capitals). No other scene of the disc
shows the key, and no game code looks it up by name. The menu's description
of the button and the game's messages that name Nintendo Wi-Fi Connection keep
their texts.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_tweaks.h b/include/mscharged_tweaks.h
index 23ba2ab..8ec21f9 100644
--- a/include/mscharged_tweaks.h
+++ b/include/mscharged_tweaks.h
@@ -289,6 +289,10 @@ bool mscharged_tweak_training_item_giant(void);
 // once, the message of the popup that says so.
 bool mscharged_tweak_online_locked(void);
 const unsigned short* mscharged_tweak_take_online_lock_message(void);
+// Recharged's names for the game's own texts (tweak patch 0097), always on:
+// the text for a localization key (the hash of its name) the FE's text
+// components show, in every language, or null to keep the game's.
+const unsigned short* mscharged_tweak_loc_text(unsigned long key);
 // Recharged's tournaments (tweak patch 0076): the game that wins one ends
 // with the tournament trophy's ceremony, as the cut online tournament's
